<title>UK: Britain's Vosper wins Qatar defence work.</title>
<headline>Britain's Vosper wins Qatar defence work.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vosper Thornycroft Holdings Plc said on Monday that it has won around one fifth of an arms package deal signed by Britain and Qatar.</p>
<p>Britain and Qatar signed an $825 million deal to supply the Gulf Arab state with armoured personel carriers, patrol boats, missiles and Hawk trainer aircraft.  </p>
<p>Vosper said the package included two Vosper Thornycroft 46- metre patrol craft &quot;representing around a fifth of the total as well as equipment from GKN, Shorts and BAe.&quot;</p>
<p>The deal signed between Britian and Qatar on Sunday involves GKN Piranha armoured personnel carriers, British Aerospace Hawk Training aircraft and Starburst missiles by Shorts Missile Systems, a joint venture between Short Brothers and France's Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>Shares in Vosper Thornycroft had risen 36p to 871 by 1139 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
